    <string name="settings_adblock_subtitle">Block ads and trackers via DNS, including YouTube ad-delivery domains. On some sites empty ad frames may remain.</string>
    <string name="settings_browser_adblock">Block banner ads in browser</string>
    <string name="settings_browser_adblock_subtitle">Requires installing a local certificate (Android will show a warning — this only affects traffic on this device, going through this app). Removes banners in Chrome cleanly instead of leaving empty boxes. Does not affect YouTube.</string>
    <string name="log_browser_adblock_disabled">Browser ad-block stopped working and was turned off automatically</string>
    <string name="log_browser_adblock_cert_untrusted">Browser ad-block certificate isn\'t trusted — reinstall it in Settings. Feature turned off.</string>
    <string name="log_browser_adblock_selftest_inconclusive">Couldn\'t verify browser ad-block this session; left off to avoid breaking browsing.</string>
    <string name="settings_browser_adblock_cert_error">Couldn\'t prepare the ad-block certificate. Please try again.</string>
    <string name="faq_title">Frequently Asked Questions</string>
    <string name="faq_section_what_title">What is this</string>
    <string name="faq_section_what_body">"Block banner ads in browser" is a deeper level of ad blocking than the basic toggle. The app runs a local proxy on your phone that not only blocks ad requests, but also cleanly hides the emptied slot on the page — banners disappear completely, with no empty gaps left behind.</string>
    <string name="faq_section_youtube_title">Why YouTube app ads aren\'t blocked</string>
    <string name="faq_section_youtube_body">Ads inside the YouTube app are embedded directly in the encrypted server response together with the video itself — there\'s no separate ad request to cut out without breaking playback. YouTube\'s app also only trusts system certificates and checks Certificate Transparency, so intercepting its traffic isn\'t possible even in theory. This feature removes banners and trackers in the browser (Chrome), not the ads inside YouTube videos.</string>
    <string name="faq_section_install_title">How to install the certificate</string>
    <string name="faq_section_install_body">After turning the toggle on, Android shows a warning that the certificate must be installed in Settings — this is normal for any app installing its own certificate, and Android does not let apps install it automatically. To finish: open this screen\'s "Share certificate file" button, save the file (e.g. to your Files app or Downloads), then go to Settings → Security → Encryption &amp; credentials → Install a certificate → CA certificate, and pick the saved file. The certificate only affects this app\'s traffic on this device, is never sent anywhere, and stays entirely local.</string>
    <string name="faq_section_broke_title">Sites stopped loading after enabling</string>
    <string name="faq_section_broke_body">If sites stop loading after enabling (a certificate error), the install wasn\'t completed. The app checks this itself on every VPN connection and automatically turns the feature off if the certificate isn\'t trusted, leaving your normal internet untouched. Just reinstall the certificate and reconnect.</string>
    <string name="faq_section_autodisabled_title">The feature turned itself off</string>
    <string name="faq_section_autodisabled_body">The app continuously checks that the built-in proxy is still alive. If it unexpectedly stops (e.g. the certificate was removed from Android settings), the feature turns itself off automatically and the browser falls back to normal internet without interruption. Just turn the toggle back on if you want it again.</string>
    <string name="faq_section_safety_title">Is this safe?</string>
    <string name="faq_section_safety_body">The certificate is generated locally on your device and never sent anywhere. Google, YouTube, Apple, Microsoft, banking apps, and government services are intentionally excluded — their secure connections are never intercepted. The feature is fully optional and can be turned off with a single toggle at any time.</string>
